pg-lake (3.4.4-1PGSTY) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Package the upstream v3.4.4 bugfix release.
  * Keep the pinned Avro, DuckDB, and duckdb-postgres source revisions unchanged.
  * Propagate Debian debug and hardening flags into vcpkg dependencies.
  * Bound vcpkg dependency parallelism to two memory-safe jobs by default.
  * Use matching target and host release-only vcpkg triplets.
  * Support an enforced no-download build after the dependency cache gate.
  * Limit the outer extension build to two jobs as well.
  * Pass that limit through the nested DuckDB install rebuild.
  * Collect generated dbgsym .deb files alongside the main packages.
  * Cache nested DuckDB compilation with full command and compiler-content keys.
  * Keep PostgreSQL bridge, LLVM bitcode, private-runtime linking, and debug maps per major.
  * Build vcpkg dependencies and the bundled DuckDB with line-table debug information only (-g1).
  * Key the vcpkg binary cache by the Debian build flags.
  * Keep PGXS modules on their pg_config flags instead of overriding CFLAGS.

 -- Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>  Sun, 06 Sep 2026 17:20:00 +0800

